@startuml 15-ephemeral-capture
' Copyright 2026 Muhammad Salah
' SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
title PortCloak — Ephemeral Clone Execution (never touch the serving instance)

actor Operator
participant "PortCloak\nOrchestrator" as O
participant "Cluster / Engine API" as API
participant "SERVING Keycloak\n(pod / container)" as LIVE #FADBD8
participant "EPHEMERAL clone\n(same image, hung)" as EPH #D5F5E3
database "Keycloak DB" as DB

Operator -> O : Capture realm "acme"

== 1. Read the shape of the serving workload (read-only) ==
O -> API : Get pod/container spec
API --> LIVE : inspect (no exec, no write)
LIVE --> O : image ref, env / envFrom, secrets,\nvolumes, serviceAccount, pull secrets,\nresources, securityContext
note right of O
  The serving instance is only ever READ.
  PortCloak never execs into it, never writes
  to its filesystem, never competes for its CPU.
end note

== 2. Materialise an ephemeral clone ==
O -> O : derive clone spec:\n- same image + env + volumes\n- command -> hang (sleep infinity)\n- <b>STRIP selector labels</b>\n- strip probes / ownerRefs / status\n- label portcloak.io/job=<id>
note right of O
  Stripping app labels is critical: an inherited
  <i>app=keycloak</i> label would make the production
  Service load-balance real traffic into the
  hung export pod.
end note
O -> API : Create Job/Pod (k8s) or Container (docker)
API -> EPH : schedule + start (hung, not serving)
EPH --> O : Running

== 3. Export inside the clone ==
O -> EPH : exec: kc.sh export ~--dir /tmp/portcloak-<id>\n~--realm acme ~--users different_files\n~--http-port <free> ~--http-management-port <free>
EPH -> DB : read realm, users, credentials,\nclients, keys, federations
DB --> EPH : rows
EPH --> O : exit code + streamed stdout/stderr

== 4. Stream artifacts out ==
O -> EPH : exec tar / CopyFromContainer
EPH --> O : realm-export.json, users-*.json\n(chunked, checksummed, resumable)

== 5. Always destroy the clone ==
O -> API : Delete Job/Pod/Container (force)
API -> EPH !! : removed
note right of API
  Cleanup runs on success AND failure.
  ttlSecondsAfterFinished + a label sweep on
  next launch reap anything orphaned by a crash.
end note

O --> Operator : artifacts + manifest + completeness

@enduml
